-- title:
--   Central character bound along the support of a twisted Hecke word
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subseteq L$ be number fields with $L/K$ Galois, let $\nu_{Z,L}$ be a Haar measure on the idele unit group $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ (taken with its Borel structure), let $D$ be an idele Galois descent datum for $L/K$, i.e. a homomorphism $\tau \mapsto D.\mathrm{act}\,\tau$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ to continuous ring automorphisms of $\mathbb{A}_L$ extending the action on $L$, and let $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ be such that every $\tau$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$. Fix a finite set $S_L$ of finite places of $L$, a homomorphism $\xi_L$ from $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ (as the top subgroup) to $\mathbb{C}^\times$ which is continuous as a $\mathbb{C}$-valued function and trivial on the principal ideles, a finite set $S$ of finite places of $K$, an archimedean factor $\varphi_a$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{R})$ and semi-local factors $\varphi_{S,v}$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$. Then for every finite set $T$ of finite places of $K$ with $\#T \ge 2$ such that no place of $L$ above a place of $T$ lies in $S_L$, every choice of extensions $w_v \mid v$, of places $w'_v$ with $(w'_v)$'s ideal equal to $\sigma$ applied to the ideal of $w_v$ for $v \in T$, of elements $\varpi_v$ of the valuation ring of $L_{w_v}$ that are irreducible and nonzero in $L_{w_v}$ for $v \in T$, of integers $n_v$ and families $r_{T,v} : \mathrm{Fin}(n_v) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(L_{w_v})$ which for $v \in T$ form a Hecke coset system for the subgroup $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathcal{O}_{w_v})$ and the element $\mathrm{diag}(\varpi_v,1)$ (each representative lies in the double coset, the representatives cover it modulo the subgroup on the right, and their cosets are pairwise distinct), and of elements $z_v \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L_{w_v})$ equal to the scalar matrix $\varpi_v \cdot 1$ for $v \in T$, there is a real $A \ge 0$ with the following property. For all exponent functions $k, j$ on the finite places of $K$, and all $\varphi : \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L) \to \mathbb{C}$, $\varphi_f : \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{L,f}) \to \mathbb{C}$ such that $\varphi$ is the semi-local factorisation at $S \cup T$ of $\varphi_a$, $\varphi_f$ and the local factors given at $v \in T$ by $x \mapsto \sum_{\iota : \mathrm{Fin}(k_v) \to \mathrm{Fin}(n_v)} \mathbf{1}_{\text{integral set}}\big((\text{semi-local component at } v \text{ of the local embedding at } w_v \text{ of } \prod_m r_{T,v}(\iota\,m) \cdot z_v^{\,j_v})^{-1} x\big)$ and at $v \notin T$ by $\varphi_{S,v}$ (so: $\varphi_a$ is a smooth compactly supported archimedean factor, $\varphi_f$ is locally constant with compact support, each local factor at a place of $S \cup T$ is locally constant with compact support, $\varphi_f(h)$ equals the product of the local factors evaluated at the semi-local components of $h$ when all components outside $S \cup T$ are integral and vanishes otherwise, and $\varphi(g) = \varphi_a(g_\infty)\varphi_f(g_f)$), and for all $t \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$, $y \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ and $z \in \mathbb{A}_L^\times$: if $\varphi\big(y^{-1} \cdot t \cdot \sigma_D(z \cdot 1 \cdot y)\big) \ne 0$, where $t$ is viewed in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$, $z \cdot 1$ is the central scalar attached to $z$ and $\sigma_D$ is the action of $\sigma$ through $D$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$, then $$\|\xi_L(z)\| \le A \prod_{v \in T} \Big(\sqrt{\|\xi_L(\det h_{w'_v})\|}^{\,k_v} \cdot \|\xi_L(\det h_{w'_v})\|^{\,j_v}\Big),$$ where $h_{w'_v} = \mathrm{heckeGen}$ at $w'_v$, the element of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ built from the uniformiser unit at $w'_v$.
--
--   This is the character-peeling step in the comparison of twisted orbital integrals: along the support of the integrand attached to a Hecke word of profile $(k_v, j_v)_{v \in T}$, the size of the central idele class character is controlled, up to a constant independent of the profile, by the character values at the Hecke symbols $\det h_{w'_v}$. It feeds the bound on sums of twisted orbital integrals [`AutomorphicForm.exists_forall_sum_integral_norm_orbital_add_weightedOrbital_le_of_isSemiLocalFactorization`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_forall_sum_integral_norm_orbital_add_weightedOrbital_le_of_isSemiLocalFactorization), and is obtained from the absolute bound on idele norms of determinants along the same support together with the invariance of the idele norm of the determinant under the $\sigma$-action and under global points.
